{
    "map": {
        "approx_num_vertices.descr": "Choose between 4 and 10,000. More vertices will improve accuracy but can extend processing time. A value of -1 will calculate all vertices. More vertices will increase accuracy but also the processing time.",
        "approx_num_vertices.title": "Approximate number of vertices",
        "description": "Computes the extent of every raster in a mosaic dataset. This tool is used when you have added or removed raster datasets from a mosaic dataset and want to recompute the footprints.",
        "edge_tolerance.descr": "<xdoc><p>Snap the footprint to the sheet edge if it is within this tolerance. Units are the same as those in the mosaic dataset coordinate system.</p><p>By default, the value is empty for which the tolerance is computed based on the pixel size corresponding to the requested resampled raster.</p><p>A value of -1 will compute the tolerance using the average pixel size of the mosaic dataset.</p></xdoc>",
        "edge_tolerance.title": "Edge tolerance",
        "in_mosaic_dataset.descr": "The mosaic dataset that contains the raster datasets whose footprints you want to compute.",
        "in_mosaic_dataset.title": "Mosaic Dataset",
        "maintain_edges.descr": "<xdoc><p>Alter the footprints of raster datasets that have been tiled and are adjacent (line up along the seams with little to no overlap).</p><ul><li>Unchecked—Remove the sheet edges from all the footprints. This is the default.</li><li>Checked—Maintain the footprints in their original state.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "maintain_edges.title": "Maintain sheet edges",
        "max_data_value.descr": "Exclude pixels with a value greater than this number.",
        "max_data_value.title": "Maximum Data Value",
        "max_sliver_size.descr": "<xdoc><p>Identify all polygons that are smaller than the square of this value. The value is specified in pixels and is based on the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Request Size</span>, not the spatial resolution of the source raster.</p><p>Regions less than the (<span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Maximum Sliver Size</span>)^2 and less than the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Minimum Thinness Ratio</span> are considered slivers and will be removed.</p></xdoc>",
        "max_sliver_size.title": "Maximum Sliver Size",
        "min_data_value.descr": "Exclude pixels with a value less than this number.",
        "min_data_value.title": "Minimum Data Value",
        "min_region_size.descr": "Avoid small holes in your imagery when using pixel values to create a mask. For example, your imagery may have a range of values from 0 to 255, and to mask clouds, you've excluded values from 245 to 255, which may cause other, noncloud pixels to be masked as well. If those areas are smaller than the number of pixels specified here, they will not be masked out.",
        "min_region_size.title": "Minimum Region Size",
        "min_thinness_ratio.descr": "<xdoc><p>Define the thinness of slivers on a scale from 0 to 1.0, where 1.0 represents a circle and 0.0 represents a polygon that approaches a straight line.</p><p>Polygons that are below both the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Maximum Sliver Size</span> and <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Minimum Thinness Ratio</span> will be removed from the footprint.</p></xdoc>",
        "min_thinness_ratio.title": "Minimum Thinness Ratio",
        "out_mosaic_dataset.title": "Updated Mosaic Dataset",
        "params.category1": "Advanced Options",
        "params.category2": "Sliver Removal Options",
        "request_size.descr": "Set the resampled extent (in columns and rows) for the raster when building footprints. Greater image resolution provides more detail in the raster dataset but increases the processing time. A value of -1 will compute the footprint at the original resolution.",
        "request_size.title": "Request Size",
        "reset_footprint.descr": "<xdoc><p>Refine the footprints using one of the following methods:</p><ul><li><span title=\"RADIOMETRY\">Radiometry</span>— Exclude pixels with a value outside of a defined range. This option is generally used to exclude border areas, which do not contain valid data. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"GEOMETRY\">Geometry</span>— Restore the footprint to its original geometry.</li><li><span title=\"COPY_TO_SIBLING\">Copy to sibling</span>— Replace the panchromatic footprint with the multispectral footprint when using a pan-sharpened raster type. This can occur when the panchromatic and multispectral images do not have identical geometries.</li><li><span title=\"NONE\">None</span>—Do not redefine the footprints.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "reset_footprint.domain.COPY_TO_SIBLING": "Copy to sibling",
        "reset_footprint.domain.GEOMETRY": "Geometry",
        "reset_footprint.domain.NONE": "None",
        "reset_footprint.domain.RADIOMETRY": "Radiometry",
        "reset_footprint.title": "Computation Method",
        "shrink_distance.descr": "<xdoc><p>Clip the footprint by this distance. This can eliminate artifacts from using lossy compression, which causes the edges of the image to overlap into NoData areas.</p><p>Shrinking of the polygon is used to counteract effects of lossy compression, which causes edges of the image to overlap into NoData areas.</p></xdoc>",
        "shrink_distance.title": "Shrink distance",
        "simplification_method.descr": "<xdoc><p>Reduce the number of vertices in the footprint to improve performance.</p><ul><li><span title=\"NONE\">None</span>—Do not limit the number of vertices. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"CONVEX_HULL\">Convex hull</span>—Use the minimum bounding box to simplify the footprint.</li><li><span title=\"ENVELOPE\">Envelope</span>—Use the envelope of each mosaic dataset item to simplify the footprint.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "simplification_method.domain.CONVEX_HULL": "Convex hull",
        "simplification_method.domain.ENVELOPE": "Envelope",
        "simplification_method.domain.NONE": "None",
        "simplification_method.title": "Simplification Method",
        "skip_derived_images.descr": "<xdoc><p>Adjust the footprints of overviews.</p><ul><li>Checked—Do not adjust the footprints of overviews. This is the default.</li><li>Unchecked—Adjust the footprints of overviews and associated raster datasets.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "skip_derived_images.title": "Skip overviews",
        "title": "Build Footprints",
        "update_boundary.descr": "<xdoc><p>Update the boundary of the mosaic dataset if you have added or removed imagery that changes the extent.</p><ul><li>Checked—Update the boundary. This is the default.</li><li>Unchecked—Do not update the boundary.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "update_boundary.title": "Update Boundary",
        "where_clause.descr": "An SQL expression to select specific raster datasets within the mosaic dataset.",
        "where_clause.title": "Query Definition"
    }
}
